# What must never reach the build context for the client image.
#
# In force when the image is built with this directory as the context, which is
# how client/Dockerfile is meant to be built:
#   docker build -t medisense-client ./client

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing secret belongs in a browser bundle, and a .env in the context is a
# secret in a layer. The two public values this build needs arrive as build
# arguments instead, where they are visible on purpose.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Installed and built output ----------------------------------------------
# node_modules is installed inside the image from the lockfile: copying the
# host's would carry platform-specific binaries built for Windows into a Linux
# image, and would defeat the layer caching the install stage exists for.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Tests and tooling -------------------------------------------------------
# None of this is part of a running server. The suite runs in CI, not in a
# production build.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
vitest.config.*
vitest.setup.*
coverage/
.vitest/
eslint.config.*

# --- Repository furniture ----------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
README.md

# --- Editor / OS -------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
